{ id:"sintering", no:"12", phase:"Electrode & electrolyte production", title:"Sintering", machine:"sintering", routes:"oxide",
  sub:"Cathode & electrolyte production", trans:1, tpage:1,
  env:{iso:"Inert gas or vacuum", dew:"no environmental reaction permitted", temp:"500–1 500 °C"},
  cost:"—", takt:"several hours",
  purpose:"Heat the cathode–electrolyte composite below its melting point so the particles grow together, densifying the layer and lowering interfacial resistance.",
  inp:"Unsintered cathode–electrolyte layer", out:"Sintered, densified layer",
  parts:[
    ["Infeed","FEED","The unsintered composite enters the furnace. Binders and pore-forming agents used earlier evaporate during this step."],
    ["Heating elements","HEAT","The 3rd edition gives a single range, 500 to 1 500 °C, with a specific temperature profile for the material. The energy input at the top of that range is a real process cost."],
    ["High temperature zone","SINTER","Mass transport is thermally activated and the particles grow together. This is what produces the final strength and density."],
    ["Sintered layer","PRODUCT","Densification reduces the resistance between electrolyte and electrode. Oxide cells are not pressed after stacking, so this is where interfacial contact has to be won."],
    ["Atmosphere","PROTECT","Inert gas or vacuum, to prevent reactions with the environment at temperature."]],
  params:["Process duration: usually several hours","Temperature: 500–1 500 °C","Specific temperature profiles","Sintering pressure — atmospheric preferred"],
  alts:["Pulsed laser sintering","Spark plasma sintering, flash sintering and similar"],
  chall:["Different sintering kinetics of the materials","Possible mechanical damage"],
  qInf:["Different sintering kinetics and physical properties of the materials","High energy input for high sintering temperatures"],
  qFeat:["Composite bonding during co-sintering","Porosity","Grain size","Avoidance of organic residues"],
  sop:["Confirm the furnace atmosphere","Load the composite on its carrier","Ramp to the sintering temperature on profile","Hold for the specified time","Cool on the controlled ramp","Check density, grain size and adhesion"] },

{ id:"stacking", no:"13", phase:"Cell assembly", title:"Stacking & compression", machine:"stacking", routes:ALL,
  sub:"Cell assembly", trans:4, tpage:1,
  env:{iso:"Dry / clean room", dew:"dry", temp:"heated pressing",},
  cost:"—", takt:"under 1 s per sheet",
  purpose:"Place the elementary cells on top of each other and press the stack so the interfaces actually touch.",
  inp:"Elementary cells", out:"Bipolar cell stack",
  parts:[
    ["Gripper mechanics","HANDLE","Grippers position each elementary cell. The gripping technique must not damage the surface — a scuffed solid electrolyte is a short."],
    ["Vacuum gripper","PICK","Position detection and alignment with a vacuum gripper is the named challenge. Positioning accuracy is under 300 µm."],
    ["Cell stack","BUILD","Because the electrolyte is solid, no separator is stacked. That is one whole material and one whole placement step removed compared with a lithium-ion cell."],
    ["Press","COMPRESS","Pressure and heat laminate the elementary cells together. With sulfidic and polymeric electrolytes this reduces grain-boundary resistance, raises ionic conductivity and lowers interfacial resistance. Oxide stacks are not pressed after stacking — they won their interface in the sintering furnace instead."],
    ["Bipolar connection","SERIES","Elementary cells can be stacked bipolarly — a series connection inside one housing. Cell voltage multiplies and only the outer collectors are needed."]],
  params:["Stacking speed under 1 s per sheet","Positioning accuracy under 300 µm","Temperature","Pressure force"],
  alts:["Continuous stacking processes","Flat winding"],
  chall:["Position detection and alignment","Absence of damage"],
  qInf:["Position detection and alignment with a vacuum gripper","Short circuits during stacking"],
  qFeat:["Positioning accuracy","Undamaged surfaces","Compressed cell layers, depending on the cell chemistry"],
  sop:["Verify the gripper contact surfaces","Set the stacking sequence and layer count","Run and monitor placement accuracy","Transfer the stack to the press","Apply pressure and temperature on profile","Check for damage before contacting"] },

