  inp:"Sealed cell", out:"Formed, aged, released cell",
  parts:[
    ["Spring contact probes","CONTACT","Type of contact is one of the three named challenges — a poor contact reads as a bad cell."],
    ["Power electronics","CYCLE","A defined C-rate for the first discharge and charge, increased successively. The current and voltage curve is the record of what happened."],
    ["Interface layer","FORM","A boundary layer forms between the electrolyte and the electrodes. It significantly influences ionic conductivity and therefore cell performance."],
    ["Aging rack","HOLD","Cells are stored in racks or towers under a controlled atmosphere while open-circuit voltage is measured at intervals."],
    ["Already charged","NOTE","With a lithium metal anode, the cell is already charged in the assembled state — a different starting point from a lithium-ion cell."],
    ["Shorter than LIB","EXPECT","Less time and cost are expected than for lithium-ion formation, and shorter aging, because stable properties are reached faster with a solid electrolyte."]],
